<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Shoprite lifts first half earnings.</title>
<headline>Shoprite lifts first half earnings.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   16.5	  vs    14.2</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     20.3	  vs    11.5</p>
<p>    Div, expected (cts)*   6.5	  vs	-</p>
<p>    Net profit	     103.34	 vs    57.21</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  152.29	 vs    91.34</p>
<p>    Tax			 47.04	 vs    32.84</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   18.09	 vs     7.64</p>
<p>    Exceptional gain	18.48	 vs    13.62 charge</p>
<p>    Turnover	     4,788.50	 vs 3,752.95</p>
<p>*Div confirmation, payment to be advised</p>
<p>Full name: Shoprite Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The retail group said that it expected satisfactory results over the next six months. Electronic point of sale systems were now in place to allow it to link up with banks and other financial institutions to provide financial services. Opportunities in other African countries continued to be explored and the group's first supermarket in Mozambique would open in June.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
